    "summary": "Universal, visual, and writing ladders. Rule: Do not optimize a lower level while a higher level remains unresolved.",
    "content": "## Universal Ladder\n\n1. Purpose\n2. Premise / claim\n3. Structure\n4. Audience effect\n5. Internal logic / construction\n6. Local execution\n7. Surface polish\n\n## Visual Ladder\n\n1. Intent\n2. Composition\n3. Value / major shape\n4. Gesture / action\n5. Construction\n6. Proportion\n7. Subject-specific structure\n8. Material\n9. Rendering\n\n## Writing Ladder\n\n1. Intent\n2. Claim / premise\n3. Argument / structure\n4. Voice / stance\n5. Rhythm\n6. Sentence / paragraph logic\n7. Clarity\n8. Mechanics\n9. Polish\n\n## Time-Based / Spatial Ladder (Deepening)\n\n1. Intent\n2. Structure over time / space\n3. Rhythm / pacing / duration\n4. Sequence / adjacency\n5. Relationship to body / viewer\n6. Material and site\n7. Technical execution\n\n## Diagnostic Rule\n\n> [!important] **Do Not Optimise a Lower Level While a Higher Level Remains Unresolved.**\n\n## Diagnostic Output Format\n\nEvery diagnosis should answer:\n\n> **The highest unresolved level is ____. The decision causing the problem is ____. I would test ____ next. I would accept / reject the result if ____.**\n\n> [!example] Diagnostic Output in Practice\n>\n> **The highest unresolved level is** composition. **The decision causing the problem is** placing the focal point at the center of the frame, which makes the image static. **I would test** moving the focal point to the upper-left third and letting the diagonal of the arm lead the eye there. **I would accept the result if** the eye enters at the focal point and stays there for at least two seconds before exploring the rest of the image.\n\n---"
