    "summary": "Directory structure, version naming (project_v01_date_status_purpose), and logs.",
    "content": "> [!tip] Use Only What You Need\n> The course contains many templates. You do not need all of them. Start with three: practice log, problem-finding log, decision log. Add others only when you feel their absence. The practice is the point. The templates are shadows of it.\n\n## Practice Log\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Date | |\n| Micro-skill | |\n| Success criterion | |\n| Reps completed | |\n| Difficulty (1–5) | |\n| Errors observed | |\n| Correction applied | |\n| Result after correction | |\n| Next session focus | |\n\n## Problem-Finding Log\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Date | |\n| Source | |\n| Observation | |\n| Question | |\n| Tension | |\n| Mode | Solve / Investigate / Reveal / Reframe / Explore / Construct |\n| Positionality | From / With / For / About |\n| Standing | Do I have it, on what basis? |\n| Possible premise | |\n| Stakes | |\n| Would I pursue? | Yes / No / Maybe |\n| Follow-up | |\n\n## Non-Instrumental Attention Log\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Date | |\n| Session type | Walk / Reading / Looking / Listening / Materials |\n| Duration | |\n| What I encountered that I was not looking for | One sentence |\n\n## Play Log\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Date | |\n| What I did | |\n| Duration | |\n| What I enjoyed | One sentence |\n\n## Calibration Log\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Date | |\n| System | |\n| Variable changed | |\n| Prediction | |\n| Confidence | % |\n| Actual | |\n| Direction of error | |\n| Magnitude of error | |\n| Explanation | |\n| Revision | |\n\n## Decision Log\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Context | |\n| Decision | |\n| Alternative | |\n| Reason | |\n| Evidence | |\n| Risk | |\n| Result | |\n| Revision | |\n\n## Conflict Log (Collaboration)\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Disagreement | |\n| Positions | |\n| Level | Premise / structure / execution / preference |\n| Mechanism | |\n| Resolution | |\n| Loss | |\n| Economic dimension | Was money, credit, or ownership at stake? |\n\n## Brief Template\n\n| Layer | Content |\n|---|---|\n| Premise | |\n| Intention | |\n| Constraints | |\n| References | |\n| Acceptance criteria | |\n| Rejection conditions | |\n| Risks and unknowns | |\n\n## Diagnosis Template\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Work | |\n| Likely intention | |\n| Highest unresolved level | |\n| Decision causing problem | |\n| Proposed intervention | |\n| Evidence that would confirm | |\n\n## Anchor Record\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Artifact | |\n| Source / provenance | |\n| Medium | |\n| Intended function | |\n| What succeeds | |\n| What fails | |\n| Mechanism | |\n| Diagnostic level | |\n| Reference class | |\n| Purpose | |\n| Accept / reject | |\n| Date added | |\n| Date revisited | |\n| Criteria changed? | |\n\n## Critique Record\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Source | |\n| Role | |\n| Feedback | |\n| Inferred problem | |\n| Maps to brief? | |\n| Blind spot? | |\n| Decision | |\n| Reasoning | |\n| Result | |\n\n## Transfer Test Record\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Prompt / situation | |\n| What I did without scaffolding | |\n| Where I hesitated | |\n| Did I import a template blindly? | |\n| What principle transferred | |\n| What new principle had to be invented | |\n\n## Teaching Feedback Record\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Session | |\n| Learner | |\n| What I supplied | |\n| What I removed | |\n| Where I was tempted to do the work | |\n| Learner's account | What they decided, what they still don't know |\n| Observer's account | Where I did the work for them |\n| My read vs their read | Gap between what I thought and what happened |\n| Revision | What I'll change next time |\n\n## Log Integrity Audit\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Log audited | |\n| Date range | |\n| Hollow entries identified | |\n| Repeating fields | |\n| Specificity change | |\n| Next audit | |\n\n## Project Archive Structure\n\n```\nproject-name/\n├── 00-problem/\n│   ├── problem-finding-log.md\n│   ├── positionality-check.md\n│   └── problem-statement.md\n├── 01-brief/\n│   ├── premise.md\n│   ├── brief.md\n│   └── acceptance-criteria.md\n├── 02-references/\n│   ├── anchor-01.md\n│   └── anchor-02.md\n├── 03-process/\n│   ├── pipeline.md\n│   ├── variable-map.md\n│   ├── calibration-log.md\n│   ├── decision-log.md\n│   └── provenance.md\n├── 04-outputs/\n│   ├── v01/\n│   ├── v02/\n│   └── final/\n├── 05-diagnosis/\n│   ├── diagnosis-01.md\n│   └── diagnosis-02.md\n├── 06-revision/\n│   ├── re-brief-decision.md\n│   └── revision-log.md\n├── 07-defense/\n│   └── defense.md\n├── 08-collaboration/ (if applicable)\n│   ├── authorship-agreement.md\n│   ├── decision-rights.md\n│   ├── economics-agreement.md\n│   └── conflict-log.md\n└── 09-reflection/\n    └── transfer-reflection.md\n```\n\n## Version Naming Convention\n\n> [!important] Versioning Is Thinking, Not File Hygiene\n> The status field records where the work is in its decision-making lifecycle, not just whether it is \"done.\"\n\n`project-name_v01_YYYY-MM-DD_status_purpose`\n\nStatus values:\n\n- `draft` — early, exploratory, not yet reviewed\n- `review` — submitted for critique, awaiting feedback\n- `approved` — decision made, moving to production\n- `final` — delivered, no further revision planned\n- `superseded` — replaced by a later version\n- `archived` — no longer active, kept for record\n\nExample: `trainpiece_v03_2026-03-15_reviewed_focal-fix`\n\n## Data Provenance Record\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Input source | |\n| License | |\n| Consent obtained? | |\n| Tool used | |\n| Tool data policy | |\n| Output license | |\n| Disclosure required? | |\n| Human contribution | |\n| Transformation applied | |\n| Reference sources | |\n| Date/version of tool | |\n| Restrictions on use | |\n\n> [!important] **Human Contribution** Is the Most Important Field\n> Provenance should not merely answer \"Where did the material come from?\" It should also answer: **What did the human actually decide, transform, construct, reject, and contribute?**\n>\n> This makes the provenance record serve the course's philosophical purpose, not merely compliance paperwork.\n\n## Collaboration Templates\n\n### Authorship Agreement\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Project | |\n| Collaborators | |\n| Credit | |\n| Ownership of output | |\n| Ownership of process / pipeline | |\n| Right to reuse | |\n| Right to disclose | |\n| Exit terms | |\n\n### Decision Rights Map\n\n| Decision type | Owner | Consultation | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| | | | |\n\n### Economics Agreement\n\n| Field | Entry |\n|---|---|\n| Revenue split | |\n| Basis (equal / weighted / role / milestone) | |\n| Credit order | |\n| Cost sharing | |\n| What counts as contribution | |\n| Handling of unequal contribution | |\n| Process / pipeline ownership | |\n| Dissolution terms | |\n| Financial authority | |\n| Dispute resolution | |\n\n---"
